  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preventing HIV/AIDS and Strengthening treatment of PLHIV - Bhutan (01-Jul-2015-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bhutan, HIV, Ministry of Health of the Royal Government of Bhutan (MOH)This program has the following goals: To reduce new HIV infections and provide continuum of care to people living with and affected by HIV (Goal of NSP 2012-2016). The objectives of this program are: Objective: To ensure that strategic information for an evidence&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201c;based response is in place, and the capacity of MoH and CSOs to monitor the response is well-developed..  Objective: To provide a comprehensive package of HIV prevention services at high coverage targeted to key affected and vulnerable populations..  Objective: To scale up HIV treatment, care and support to 90% of those diagnosed with the virus in order to reduce mortality and morbidity, and leverage the prevention effects of early treatment..  Objective: To scale up HTC among key affected and vulnerable populations by adopting an intensified case-finding approach in order to diagnose at least 60% of those estimated to be living with HIV in Bhutan..  Objective: To strengthen health and community system to deliver an equitable, gender sensitive and sustainable response.</narrative>
  </description>
